  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Second Tranche of the Spanish Carbon Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Fund will stimulate capital flows for sustainable development in accordance with the UN Framework Convention on Climate Change and the Kyoto Protocol. Based on the implementation of Projects and the creation and management of carbon assets in accordance with the Marrakesh Accords of the Kyoto Protocol, the Fund will also enhance participants&apos; knowledge of carbon finance as a tool to reduce the costs of implementing obligations arising from the Kyoto Protocol, help client countries achieve sustainable development, and achieve a global environmental benefit. This is a second Tranche to the Spanish Carbon Fund whose purpose is to give continuity to the strategy of buying emission reductions and to serve as an investment bridge between the first tranche of the Spanish Carbon Fund and the new initiatives such as the Carbon Partnership Facility. The Spanish Government will be able to participate in the CPF initiative; however it will take some time for this fund to become operational as it is still under design. Thus the Second Tranche of SCF will act as an interim mechanism to allow the Spanish Government purchase emission reductions and hence comply with their Kyoto Protocol obligations. In addition, the CPF is designed primarily to but emission reductions generated after 2012 whilst the Second Tranche of SCF will purchase emission reductions generated both, before and after, 2012.</narrative>
  </description>
